⚠️ Key Issues & Improvements

1. ❌ Avoid using End

Using End immediately stops all VBA execution and can cause:

Variables not being released properly

Other macros to fail unexpectedly


✅ Use Exit Sub instead


---

2. 🔁 Remove Hard-Coded Sheet References

You already assigned:

Set ws = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(1)

But later you still use:

ThisWorkbook.Sheets("Sheet1")

This creates maintenance problems if the sheet name changes.

✅ Use ws consistently


---

3. 📂 Validate File vs Folder (Important!)

Dir(path) behaves differently depending on:

File path

Folder path


If B5 is meant to be a folder, your current check may fail.

✅ Use Dir(path, vbDirectory) for folders


---

4. 🎯 Centralize the Highlight Range

Hardcoding "B5:L5" multiple times makes updates harder.

✅ Store it in a variable


---

5. ♻️ Make the Sub Reusable (Optional but Recommended)

Return True/False so other macros can call it.


